# Normalise line endings so the repository is byte-identical on every machine.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites the LF blobs
# stored in git into CRLF on disk, and prettier -- which runs as an ESLint rule
# via eslint-plugin-prettier -- then reports every single line of every file as
# a `Delete ␍` error. CI runs on ubuntu and passes; a local `npm run lint` fails
# with ~1100 phantom errors. `* text=auto eol=lf` pins LF in the working tree
# everywhere, so local and CI results match.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
